> They need to be hidden sometimes.  Simple users don't need to know about everything, like ownership of files.  Or be prepared for them to make a mess, like storing all their e-mail inside an attribute on an e-mail icon.
> 
I agree they should be hidden for some users.  Do you think a good 
solution would be to put these things in a directory named 
"permissions", "security-settings" or something like that, to make it 
obvious what their use is, while still allowing the curious to easily 
grasp why they exist?  The filemanager could hide those directories if 
desired.


